 "notes": "No district is above the alert threshold today. Ranks are among the 6 of 20 districts the satellite imaged this cycle; the rest carry no score. The score is a ranking score, not a calibrated probability: it has not been fitted to a reliability curve, so compare districts against each other and read the tier, rather than reading the number as a chance of flooding. Rain shown alongside is Open-Meteo (ERA5 archive + forecast model, keyless, CC-BY 4.0) and is page context, not a model input. Forecast inputs are satellite flood history only: district priors, observed extent now and over three days, position in the season, neighbouring districts, the district-week climatology, and recent flooding decaying across the district graph. Rainfall was tested as a feature family and did not improve the forecast, so it is not an input; reservoir storage is not an input either. Both appear below as context only and do not move the score. Reservoir context is unavailable: the BBMB dams (Bhakra, Pong, Ranjit Sagar) stopped reporting to the CWC data.gov.in feed in Jul 2025 and carry no 2026 rows. Rain context summed over 1/1 elapsed days of the window. GFM: 1 of 1 current-window days returned data, 1 of those carried flood pixels; antecedent window 5/10 returned (~900 px grid, permanent water removed). Coverage is decided by the Sentinel-1 acquisition footprint, not by whether a tile returned: 6 of 20 districts were imaged across at least 95% of their area over the window. Districts with no pass are published without a score rather than as dry."
